# Pre-push CI

When the user asks to **commit and push**, **push**, or **create a pull
request**, follow `.cursor/skills/pre-push-ci/SKILL.md` before pushing.

- Run `./tools/ci-local.sh` (the local stand-in for the `version`, `backend`,
  and `admin` GitHub Actions jobs, plus a NuGet vulnerability check).
- Fix failures and re-run until it passes.
- Rebuild the admin bundle and stage `src/Raytha.Web/wwwroot/raytha` when
  anything under `src/admin` changed (RFC-0006).
- Bump `VERSION` in the same change (RFC-0012).
- Do not push a red tree.
- Commit-only requests do not require this.
